    {
      "id": "claim_337b827417ac48b78c1348c6ade21aed",
      "statement": "Release kind semantics: `minor` bumps Y and resets Z to land vX.Y.0; `patch` ships development's current X.Y.Z unchanged (the hotfix fast path, so main is NOT always X.Y.0); an explicit X.Y.Z sets that exact version with no bump dance. Because patch publishes whatever development currently holds, land only the fix first if development carries unreleased work.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L39-L39",
