    {
      "id": "claim_6d8932fa2dd348fc962f082cda62150c",
      "statement": "`just sync` merges development into main between releases WITHOUT cutting a release: no version bump, no CHANGELOG roll, and no tag, so the release workflow (which triggers on v* tags) is not fired; it creates a single `chore: sync development into main` first-parent merge and then fast-forwards development back so the next release still merges cleanly.",
      "evidence": [
