    {
      "id": "claim_ff0e3467838d4921ad943ae735725443",
      "statement": "Branch model: feature/fix/docs/chore/poc branches are cut from development (never main, which receives releases only and must never be a PR target), PRs target development, release merges go development→main, and merged branches are deleted (GitHub auto-delete). Names are <prefix>/<slug> keyed to what the work IS (feature/=feat, fix/=fix, docs/=docs, chore/=chore/ci/build/refactor/perf/style/test, poc/=anything), enforced by scripts/check-branch-name.sh in the pre-commit hook (shape only) and in CI (substantive commit-type check; forks skipped); never bump Cargo.toml on a non-development branch — versioning is automated.",
      "evidence": [
